            <div xml:id="d201">

                <pb facs="0949" n="907" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76v35/pg907"/>

                <head>201. Memorandum for the Record<anchor n="1" xml:id="d201-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1975-04-04">April 4, 1975</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Ad Hoc 40 Committee Meeting on MATADOR </item>
                </list>
                <p>On Friday, 28 March 1975, an ad hoc meeting of the 40 Committee was held
                    following a meeting of the National Security Council.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d201-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>General Scowcroft reported that Director Colby distributed a paper<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d201-f3"/> on MATADOR reflecting his reluctant conclusion that “it
                    is inadvisable to undertake a second mission” [<hi rendition="#italic">less than
                        1 line not declassified</hi>]–0253/75). It was decided to continue
                    preparations for a second mission.</p>
                <p>Mr. Colby reported that Secretary of Defense Schlesinger, Dr. Kissinger, Mr.
                    Clements, Mr. Sisco, General Brown, and General Scowcroft joined him at the
                    meeting of the Committee. Secretary Schlesinger thought it possible to attempt a
                    second mission, depending upon assessment of Soviet reactions, and therefore no
                    decision on whether to <pb facs="0950" n="908" xml:id="pg908"/> try a second
                    operation should be made yet. Mr. Colby said Secretary Schlesinger’s <hi
                        rendition="#italic">views were persuasive</hi>.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed> Rob Roy Ratliff </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d201-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d201-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Security Council Files, Ford Administration Intelligence Files,
                    40 Committee Meetings, Minutes/Approvals, 1975. Top Secret; [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">codeword not declassified</hi>]; MATADOR. No
                    distribution. Drafted by Ratliff.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d201-f2" n="2" xml:id="d201-f2-content">
                <p>The NSC met on March 28 to discuss Middle East Policy. The record of the meeting
                    is printed as <ref target="frus1969-76v26#d166">Document 166 in <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1969–1976, Vol. XXVI,
                        Arab-Israeli Dispute, 1974–1976</ref>.</p>
            </note>
